Ceramic grinding cores are made of inorganic materials such as alumina which are sintered at temperatures above 1300 degrees Celsius. The special properties of the materials make the ceramic grinding cores have the characteristics of high hardness, wear resistance, fast heat dissipation, corrosion resistance, safety and environmental protection, perfect for the defects of plastic or metal grinding cores.
The grinding core of the grinder will generate heat during the grinding process. Compared with metal or plastic grinding cores, the ceramic grinding core will not produce too much heat due to the characteristics of heat conduction, which will not affect the raw natural taste of the ingredients.
Ceramic grinding core products are mainly divided into two types of conical and flat structures. The products are widely used in various types of manual or electric grinding machines in households, usually used for grinding coffee, sea salt, pepper and other spices and various small grains, it has been an important kitchen tool for families.
