News - Ready to Learn More about CNC machine?
Ready to Learn More about CNC machine? News
The CNC process is the abbreviation of “computer numerical control”, which contrasts with the limitations of manual control, thus replacing the limitations of manual control. In manual control, the on-site operator is required to prompt and guide the processing through joysticks, buttons, and wheels Tool commands.
Convert CAD files to CNC code: As CAD files can be used in many applications, designers need to convert CAD drawings into CNC compatible files. They can use programs such as computer-aided manufacturing (CAM) software to change the CAD format to CNC format.
Process execution: After the files and machine tools are prepared, the CNC operator can execute the final process. They start the program and then guide the machine through the whole process.
Working in CAD: Designers use computer-aided design (CAD) software to create 2D or 3D engineering drawings. The file includes specifications such as structure and dimensions, which will tell the CNC machine how to create the part.
Machine preparation: After operators have readable files, they can set up the machine by themselves. They connect the appropriate workpieces and tools to make the program execute correctly.
When designers and operators complete this process correctly, CNC machine tools can perform their tasks efficiently and accurately.
