In principle, ultrasonic fingerprint recognition technology is based on ultrasonic waves, which are transmitted through sensors to the surface of the finger and receive echoes. The density difference between the skin and air on the fingerprint's surface was then used to build a 3D image of the fingerprint's unique valleys and ridges, which was then matched to the image stored in the phone.
