News - How are pullovers, sweatshirts & hoodies different?
When it comes to winter outerwear, we often get quite muddled up about what goes with what. So many of us reach out for a pullover or a frontline hoodie without giving a second thought about styling it right.
For instance, an oversized pullover can look amazing with clingy bottoms or something that accents your frame; whereas, a hoodie may need something rather different, depending on its silhouette and fall. You can wear a sweatshirt with a skirt any day, but styling a hoodie with a skirt can be really tricky.
The reason sweatshirts are so popular with women all across the world is because they are the definition of easy casuals; you can literally throw it on and team it with a pair of denim, and wear it to work, to brunch or even to go clubbing.
A pullover is typically apparel that you wear by pulling it over your head. And though it’s one of the most widely-used winter wardrobe staples, the pullover is quite difficult to style.
One of the most popular kinds of pullover is the hooded one as it resembles a hoodie, but it is usually much cozier and snug. Pullovers usually have an androgynous quality about them, which means that they can usually be worn by both men and women effortlessly.
It is important to understand the difference between the different vibes which a pullover, a sweatshirt, and a hoodie bring. A sweatshirt is very multi-faceted and can get into any sartorial situation.
