The hard rail is sliding friction, which belongs to surface contact. The contact surface is large, the friction force is large, and the speed of fast movement is slow.
When machining cast iron and steel castings, the amount of cutting tool is large, the cutting force is relatively large, and the vibration is relatively severe. Because the hard rail surface is in contact with the surface, the contact surface is large, and the shock absorption is relatively good, which can not only ensure the processing efficiency but also ensure the processing efficiency.
In short, when machining cast workpieces, hard rails are better, especially when roughing and finishing are done together. If only finish machining is done, the line rail is good, and the line rail moves quickly, which can save non-processing time in mass processing.
