Perhaps we are all unconsciously part of a great undertaking - and indeed one that is characterized by enormous momentum. Is it chipped by a Masonic world government?
But no - we just break the record in experiencing more and more "ends of the world" every year. And there's no end in sight (ba dum tss).
Nevertheless, whenever similar stories spread across the Internet at the speed of Usain Bolt at the peak of his career, there are debates that phew is, we lived to see it - this is the end of the world, the end of history, the end of life, the absolute "the end", the twilight of history, the last twists of all the fate of railways. We are probably just crazy about such topics.
Of course, the process known as the Cretaceous extinction not only affected T-Rex with his buddies and was long-term, but it was a kind of burying (altogether often literally) of ancient earthly life.
He had various followers, but the real fun began at the turn of the millennium. Have you ever wondered why we celebrate the end of each year with the name of New Year's Eve?
Honestly, I was already walking in this valley of tears, but I was only six years old, so my biggest concern was to watch the new episode of "Ed, Edd and Eddy", not whether all the computers would crash. So I don't remember the whole thing exactly, but the more I read about it, the more I got the impression that it was really - as the Japanese say - a "real deal".
The global catastrophe, of course, did not happen - at best some displays at the railway stations had a moment of confusion with the jumble, but everything was back to normal in the end. Well, but who forbids human brothers from getting excited about the coming millennium?
How would this come about? This probably has not been unequivocally established, because dozens of theories have emerged, each more fanciful than the previous one.
As for the good things - I experienced one of the best music concerts in my life on December 21, 2012, in the unforgettable club "Za Mostem" in Sosnowiec. The band that was performing on stage at the time was called… well, of course, the End of the World, so it was magical in itself.
There is no need to panic, especially every few months on average. Of course, there will be the physical end of the world someday - in about 10 billion years, when the death of the Sun will begin, which will change first into a red giant, then into a white dwarf, etc.
