In the article I will present the process of adding unofficial integration (Custom Component) to Home Assistant on the example of integration using eWeLink cloud services, and as a result allowing us to control Sonoff devices without changing their firmware.
Home Assistant - integration with the IKEA Tradfri system
Below, on the example of IKEA Tradfri bulbs, I will show how to use this integration. Test configuration: Home Assistant 0.102.3, system ...
Home Assistant it has a lot of official integrations that come with it, ready to use. They do not require additional installation and updating from us - they are updated along with the system.
Despite such a large collection (currently 1540 extensions), due to the pace of world development IoT, there is a need to create further integrations as part of the Home Assistant, not only to support other devices, but also related to the use of various internet services, algorithms, automation, etc. New, unofficial integrations are being created, written by the Home Assistant community.
Below I will present the process of adding unofficial integration to Home Assistant on the example of integration using eWeLink cloud services, and as a result allowing us to control devices Sonoffwithout changing their firmware. I have added eWeLink to the application switch Sonoff T4EU1C (without Neutral wire).
Because it is an integration with the eWeLink service, for it to make sense, you must first create an account in the eWeLink application and add a device to it.
and download the .zip archive with the necessary files. Then unpack the archive to disk.
We make sure that we have installed and configured the add-on Samba share.
It happens, however, that integration (official or not) merges immediately after WiFi with the device data in our local network. It is then required to know the IP address of this device and it is recommended to assign this address permanently to our router.
Most often on the GitHub website with selected integration there is a manual in which the author describes in detail the section that should be added to the configuration file. This section should be added to activate previously loaded integration.
After installing the add-on, in its settings it is enough to select "Show in sidebar" to have easy access to it from the menu Home Assistant. In addition, we select the configuration file, modify it in accordance with the rest of the instructions, and save.
After restarting Home Assistant, compatible Sonoff devices should now be available in Entities:
In the main menu "Overview", using the built-in wizard or by manually editing the file, we can add the Sonoff switch card.
